# One rule: everything git considers text is stored and checked out with LF.
#
# Added 2026-08-31. Before this file, the repo had no line-ending policy and
# core.autocrlf=false, so any tool that rewrote a file on Windows flipped it to
# CRLF and git recorded every line as changed. That made diffs unreadable and hid
# real edits: the R1.5 commit looked like a 20-file mass edit but was ~20 one-line
# changes, and R1.1/R1.6 showed 364/249 and 434/364 line diffs that were actually
# 138/23 and 84/14. Reviewing a change you cannot see is the failure this prevents.
#
# LF for .ps1 too — PowerShell reads LF scripts fine, and one rule with no
# exceptions is easier to keep than four.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.ttf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.zip binary
